ning  about not having flying cars that  probably means they're just complaining  about not having this the amazing and  entirely fictional hoverboard became an  instant sensation as soon as it appeared  and 80s and 90s kids have spent decades  demanding that science find a way to  catch up to this fantasy and while 2015  saw the popularization of dumb devices  called hoverboards that didn't actually  you know hover they're still hope in  August 2015 Lexus yes the car company  picked up the torch and created  hoverboard that actually hovers the  catch is that it needs a specifically  designed track and won't be  mass-produced as it was only created for  a commercial  then there's the startup arks PACs which  created the Hendo hoverboard while  videos of the ride show that the board  doesn't perform as well as the ones in  the movie it's enough for us to say that  hoverboards do in fact exist just don't  take it on the water  Cubs win yes in the 80s the thought of  the Cubs actually breaking their  decades-long World Series drought was  only slightly less absurd than them  actually doing so in the movies  futuristic setting the gag about the  Cubs finally taking the title in 2015  got a lot of laughs but it very nearly  came true in 2016 the Cubs won the World  Series in dramatic fashion taking game 7  into extra innings before squeaking out  a one-run victory over the Cleveland  Indians the fact that it all happened a  year after the movie predicted was noted  by none other than Michael J Fox who  added a couple of slacks when he  congratulated the team via Twitter  President Trump when Back to the Future  Part 2 was released businessman  Donald Trump had accrued a certain  measure of success but he was mostly  known to people in the New York area  most of them watched the movie without  ever suspecting that the future version  of Biff who uses his ill-gotten wealth  to build a casino empire that serves as  a springboard into political power was  based on the mogul 